WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.390
- The best thing about the iPhone Air

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:06.240
is actually how much it
seems to have freed Apple up

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.363
to make the Pro phones even more pro.

00:00:10.432 --> 00:00:14.182
(slow dramatic techno music)

00:00:22.936 --> 00:00:27.519
(slow dramatic techno music continues)

00:00:35.893 --> 00:00:40.020
(slow dramatic techno music fading)

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:41.190
Have you noticed that?

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:44.250
These new Pro phones are
thicker than last year,

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.140
more room inside for bigger batteries,

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:48.660
and a vapor chamber, and a bigger camera.

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:51.390
It's not quite on the
level of the Ultra phones,

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:54.480
but this is the most maximalist

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:57.660
that an iPhone has ever
felt, and I like it.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:59.160
But also, let me let you in

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.620
on a little not-so-secret secret.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:04.980
The Pro phone is always
the best selling one.

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:08.190
Like this year, the iPhone
Air is the most interesting

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:10.800
and it's getting the most YouTube
clicks and the most views,

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:13.830
but then the Base 17 is
more than ever the one

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:17.160
that most people should
get and the best deal.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:20.430
But it turns out the
Pro Max, specifically,

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:24.000
by far, is the most
popular, by sales numbers.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.920
I was gonna try to find a
way to show you guys this,

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:27.420
you know, channel sponsor Dbrand,

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:31.980
they make a accessory for
every single model of iPhone,

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:35.610
and so their sales distributions
kind of match Apple's.

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:38.193
And this is the distribution this year.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:42.090
Over half our Pro Maxes,
and between the two Pros,

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:44.130
that's like 90% of orders.

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:46.980
So yeah, it's fun to watch
Apple kind of walk this line

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:49.800
between being a more pro
phone than ever before

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:53.100
and this maximalist new design
and everything they're doing,

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:56.970
but also, being literally
the most mainstream phone

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:57.803
of all-time.

00:01:57.803 --> 00:01:58.636
Like the cameras.

00:01:58.636 --> 00:01:59.469
Might as well start there, right?

00:01:59.469 --> 00:02:01.830
The cameras are the most pro thing

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:04.230
about the Pro iPhone every year.

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:07.320
And on one hand, no professional
would say, "Oh yeah,

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:10.350
thank gosh I have eight
lenses now in my smartphone,"

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:12.900
like Apple seems to want us to believe.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:14.970
It clearly has three.

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:16.860
But, the three cameras you get

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:18.630
are more evenly matched than ever.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:21.150
The primary and ultra-wide
are essentially unchanged

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:23.640
from last year, but the
telephoto gets a big update.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:26.070
It's now also a 48-megapixel camera

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:28.170
and it's a 4X telephoto lens.

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:31.140
Last year was a 5X but only 12-megapixels.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:33.900
So, this new one feels
like a more natural,

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.280
portrait focal length.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:37.320
It's roughly a hundred
millimeter equivalent

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:40.350
and all of your zoom shots
will have much more detail

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:44.220
and much less noise, thanks to
the sensor being much larger

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:45.960
and much higher resolution.

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:47.160
Now, I will give them credit

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:50.490
for the specific 2X zoom increments,

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:53.760
because while they are
not actually new lenses,

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:56.190
they do specifically process
each of the images shot

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:59.580
in a 2X crop to be slightly
sharper and better looking

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:02.760
than just a pure digital crop
on the middle of the sensor.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:06.030
So, you know, it's not the
level of a pure optical zoom,

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:07.590
but it's better than nothing.

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:09.390
So, I don't know why they only do it

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:10.800
at these focal lengths, honestly.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:13.290
Either way, it's a really
nice total package now.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.540
Three matching 48-megapixel cameras,

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.610
all of which are super reliable,

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:20.160
just as good for casual
shooters as they are

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:22.770
for people who depend on
their iPhone for work,

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:25.680
or maybe who happen to have
an entire YouTube channel

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:29.219
about cars that they happen
to shoot all on smartphones.

00:03:29.219 --> 00:03:30.750
(clears throat) Yeah.

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:32.700
Electric G Wagon review
coming to "Auto Focus",

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:34.740
shot on iPhone 17 Pro very soon.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:36.090
I do still kind of find myself wishing

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:37.620
they made some other improvements,

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:40.470
like the point light problem at night

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:41.430
when you shoot in the dark

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:43.470
and those little flares always show up.

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:45.240
They haven't fixed that at all.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:46.920
Or even adding 8K video support.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:49.950
There's a two terabyte iPhone model now.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:53.280
I feel like 8K video is just
a flip of a switch away,

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:55.140
but not this year.

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:57.090
But you know, the changes
are stacked up nicely

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:59.040
over the years from older Pro phones

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:00.870
like the 13 Pro and the 14 Pro.

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:04.290
It's not a huge difference
versus last year, but it's nice.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:08.610
Also, what you're watching
right now is ProRes raw footage

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:10.680
from the iPhone 17 Pro,

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:12.120
which I was particularly excited about

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:15.600
because that means I can go
into the new Final Cut Pro 11.2,

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:19.440
I think it is, and I
can literally change ISO

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:23.910
and white balance after I
shoot, which is very useful.

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:26.610
Also, the file sizes are huge.

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:28.230
And there's even another
Pro feature that they added

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:29.670
that they couldn't brand for themselves

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:32.190
because pros already use it and named it,

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:33.660
and that's genlock support,

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:35.850
which basically lets
devices talk to each other

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:37.590
so that they can stay in sync over large,

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:38.880
multi-device shoots.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:39.713
Pretty sick.

00:04:39.713 --> 00:04:43.590
And also the selfie cameras
are more pro than ever

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:45.930
more about that in the 17 Base review.

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:47.550
But yeah, a lot going on with cameras.

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:48.870
So let's be real, 95% of people

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:50.640
who get these phones are
just gonna point and shoot

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.040
and these are more capable and
reliable than ever for that.

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:56.040
If you want more in-depth
stuff on shooting

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:57.720
like professionally with this camera,

00:04:57.720 --> 00:04:59.370
you can check out Tyler Stalman's review,

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:00.450
which I'll link below.

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:02.400
It's really in-depth and
he shot the whole thing

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.690
also on the iPhone.

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:05.430
My favorite thing about
this new Pro iPhone though

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:07.380
is actually the new design.

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:10.500
It's not often that the newest
iPhones actually change a lot

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:12.210
and get thicker and heavier,

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:13.560
but like I said, I
think that's kind of one

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:14.880
of the best things about them coming out

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:18.060
with a separate phone that's
designed just to be super thin,

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:21.480
so that if you want a thin
phone, go get the Air.

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:22.590
But if you don't care about that,

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:24.240
if that's not one of your priorities,

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:25.320
then here's the new Pro,

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:27.420
which goes the other
direction and isn't afraid

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:29.040
of a few extra fractions of an inch.

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:33.630
And I love that it's an all
uni-body metal jacket now.

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:35.820
This is not a glass sandwich anymore.

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:38.310
Literally, the whole body
of the phone is metal now

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:41.700
with glass cutouts at the
back for wireless charging,

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:44.550
and then at the top for those
millimeter wave antenna.

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:46.590
This makes it more durable,

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:48.930
it makes more room inside
for a bigger battery,

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:49.950
which we'll get to in a second,

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:52.890
and there's enough room
for a vapor chamber

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:54.570
for the first time ever in an iPhone.

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:56.700
And then the new plateau at the top,

00:05:56.700 --> 00:05:57.690
I actually think it's great.

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.760
This is where I've been
putting my index finger

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:02.250
on Android phones for years.

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:05.370
It's like a natural resting
spot to hold up the phone.

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:06.840
Same thing with this one now.

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:08.550
And Corning's Ceramic Shield too,

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:11.010
in case you haven't already
heard, is also clearly awesome

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:13.170
for preventing scratches
to the front glass.

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:18.170
A couple of nitpicks though,
no black color Pro phone?

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:20.393
You sickos.

00:06:20.393 --> 00:06:22.380
This is like one of those weird things

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:24.210
that it feels like Apple's
doing just spite me,

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:25.560
where they're making a bunch of products

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:28.290
that should have a
black version but don't.

00:06:28.290 --> 00:06:29.970
Like the new MacBook Airs come in silver,

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:33.300
and starlight, and sky
blue, and dark blue.

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:34.500
But no black?

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:36.900
And then the AirPods
Max refresh also comes

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:39.810
in a bunch of colors, and
dark blue, but no black.

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:43.890
We need a dark neutral,
especially because the color

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:46.380
that you pick actually shows up

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:48.600
around the front bezel of the phone.

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:50.760
So you see the color
you pick all the time.

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:52.650
It makes the orange and silver

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:55.133
that much more annoying to me.

00:06:55.133 --> 00:06:56.430
(sighs) I told you it was a nitpick.

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:57.930
But then you've probably
also already seen the chatter

00:06:57.930 --> 00:07:01.380
about Scratchgate, which
is just how easily it seems

00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:03.690
like the anodization layer on top

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:05.580
of the aluminum seems to scratch off

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:08.910
and then reveal the raw
silver aluminum underneath it.

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:11.910
And I kind of don't really
know what to make of this yet.

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:13.650
I feel like this has come up before

00:07:13.650 --> 00:07:16.320
with a lot of darker
anodized aluminum phones.

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:18.660
And as a person who rocks
the phone with no case,

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:20.730
I haven't had any issues
with the one I'm using.

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:21.930
I've been tossing it around.

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:24.150
But the JerryRigEverything
test has revealed

00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:26.580
that the weakest part that
you could get scratched

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:29.610
or dinged is gonna be around
the tightest corner radii,

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:31.290
like around the camera plateau.

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:33.180
So we'll see how many phones
this ends up affecting.

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:35.100
But we gotta talk about
the insides of this phone

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:37.530
because the redesign is one thing,

00:07:37.530 --> 00:07:39.930
but there's even more
going on under the surface.

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:43.350
The A19 Pro chip,
shocker, is pretty great.

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:46.320
It's benchmarked around 20%
faster than the last generation

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:49.830
and when paired with iOS
26 and 12 gigs of RAM now,

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:53.490
these phones feel really quick
and snappy, which is great.

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:56.220
But the extra thickness has also made room

00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:58.770
for a vapor chamber for the first time,

00:07:58.770 --> 00:08:01.650
and it's actually made a real
difference to the thermals

00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:02.940
and the behavior of this phone.

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:05.100
Big shout out to HGX Studio, YouTuber,

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:07.830
who is able to put thermal
cameras on these phones

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:10.230
under load and really visualize this,

00:08:10.230 --> 00:08:12.360
but especially compared to the Air,

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:15.030
these phones rarely got any more

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:16.980
than slightly warm to the touch for me.

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:18.420
And as a result, they were able

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:21.720
to actually hold higher frame
rates longer while gaming

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:23.730
and keep the display brightness higher

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:25.680
when recording videos for a long time.

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:27.210
Check out the rest of his
video too, by the way.

00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:29.670
It's freaking incredibly well done.

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:33.000
But, it also reminded me about
why, in the Android world,

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:35.460
like gaming phones kind
of have the same effect.

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:38.310
The stuff that makes a
gaming phone really good,

00:08:38.310 --> 00:08:40.710
like better speakers
and better performance,

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:43.590
and better screen and big batteries,

00:08:43.590 --> 00:08:47.130
well, all that stuff is
awesome for regular use too.

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:48.960
And it's the same deal for the Pro iPhone.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:52.470
The stuff that makes a
really good Pro iPhone,

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:55.710
like the improved display,
and the much better cameras,

00:08:55.710 --> 00:08:58.050
and the thicker, better
build with improved cooling

00:08:58.050 --> 00:08:59.490
for shooting videos longer,

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:01.560
and better sustained performance, yeah,

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:05.130
it turns out the masses
buying iPhone 17 Pro Max

00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:08.850
also really enjoy nicer screens,
cameras, and batteries too.

00:09:08.850 --> 00:09:09.683
Not a surprise.

00:09:09.683 --> 00:09:12.210
And we've all been saying for years, "Hey,

00:09:12.210 --> 00:09:15.720
just make a thicker phone
and put more battery in it."

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:17.460
I just really feel like
this is another place

00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:20.490
where having an iPhone Air
focusing on getting super thin,

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:23.430
let them feel free to go
the total other direction

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:24.330
with the other phones

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:26.160
because if they're gonna
claim the iPhone Air

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:28.830
is all-day battery life, then great,

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:31.770
every single other phone in
the lineup gets even thicker

00:09:31.770 --> 00:09:33.120
with bigger batteries.

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:37.410
So the 17 Pro has a 20%
bigger battery than last year,

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:40.110
and the Pro Max actually cracks
the 5,000 milliamp hour mark

00:09:40.110 --> 00:09:43.530
for the first time ever,
which is great in iPhone land,

00:09:43.530 --> 00:09:45.150
and also 40 watt charging now.

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:47.400
So that's half battery in 20 minutes.

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:49.890
To Apple, that's a big deal.

00:09:49.890 --> 00:09:52.170
We welcome a 20%
year-over-year improvement.

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:54.270
Now in Android land, obviously it's,

00:09:54.270 --> 00:09:55.290
it kind of looks like nothing,

00:09:55.290 --> 00:09:56.970
like it's nowhere near the Ultra phones

00:09:56.970 --> 00:10:00.030
with 6,000 milliamp hour
silicon carbon batteries

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:02.010
and 100-watt charging and all that.

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:04.890
But, for a phone that ships in the volume

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:08.160
that the iPhone does, very
happy to see that sort

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:09.690
of improvement when last year's phone

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:11.010
already had really good battery.

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:12.390
The iPhone is also very efficient.

00:10:12.390 --> 00:10:14.610
So I am getting a nice five plus hours

00:10:14.610 --> 00:10:17.610
of screen on time every day
on not even the bigger phone,

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:20.010
and it's lasting all day
with 30+ percent left.

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:20.940
So, I'm loving it.

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:23.910
And then, there's just all sorts
of other little things too,

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:25.470
like with this screen,

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:27.240
I think this is the first
generation of iPhone

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:29.790
that's had a toggle for PWM dimming.

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:31.680
Now it's buried in the
accessibility settings,

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:33.330
but you can search and find it,

00:10:33.330 --> 00:10:36.750
and that is very welcome to many people.

00:10:36.750 --> 00:10:38.790
And there's also a slightly noticeable

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:41.460
but better-than-nothing
anti-reflective coating.

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:42.293
But more importantly,

00:10:42.293 --> 00:10:43.590
the display gets slightly brighter now

00:10:43.590 --> 00:10:44.430
and I noticed that.

00:10:44.430 --> 00:10:46.710
It's up to 3000 nits peak.

00:10:46.710 --> 00:10:50.400
And satellite connectivity has
expanded to cover messaging

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:52.500
and location sharing too
now, which is useful.

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:54.360
So at the end of the day, the paradox is

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:58.860
that making the Pro iPhones more pro

00:10:58.860 --> 00:11:01.530
is actually better for the masses.

00:11:01.530 --> 00:11:05.370
And this is the best one yet,
it's the most freed one yet.

00:11:05.370 --> 00:11:06.840
And I think, you know,
when they eventually,

00:11:06.840 --> 00:11:09.000
if they make some iPhone
Ultra at some point,

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:11.490
I'll probably still want
all of that over this.

00:11:11.490 --> 00:11:13.470
But for now, this is good stuff.

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:15.510
Now if you are thinking
about getting an iPhone 17

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:17.790
but you are concerned
about those scratches,

00:11:17.790 --> 00:11:20.400
then channel sponsor Dbrand
